2
00:00:47.308 --> 00:00:49.982
No!

3
00:00:50.006 --> 00:00:51.897
My god! God! No! Please!

4
00:00:51.921 --> 00:00:53.662
- Shh! Enough!
- No. please!

5
00:00:53.792 --> 00:00:54.900
- Just behave!
- No!

6
00:00:58.884 --> 00:00:59.884
Damn it!

7
00:01:03.237 --> 00:01:05.084
What the hell. Alice?

8
00:01:05.108 --> 00:01:06.153
Damn it. Josh!

9
00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:07.695
- Stay in character!
- Well. I'm sorry!

10
00:01:07.719 --> 00:01:08.740
I just didn't expect you to get so rough!

11
00:01:08.764 --> 00:01:10.002
Is my nose bleeding?

12
00:01:10.026 --> 00:01:11.743
- No. it is not bleeding.
- Damn it.

13
00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:12.918
It's definitely gonna bruise.

14
00:01:12.942 --> 00:01:14.180
I have to present to clients on Monday.

15
00:01:14.204 --> 00:01:15.225
This was a stupid
idea. Let's just forget it.

16
00:01:15.249 --> 00:01:16.574
No. no. Wait. wait. wait. wait.

17
00:01:16.598 --> 00:01:17.902
I've got this. Let me try again.

18
00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.256
I'm gonna ravage you.

19
00:01:22.386 --> 00:01:23.755
Gross.

20
00:01:23.779 --> 00:01:24.669
Well. I'm sorry.

21
00:01:24.693 --> 00:01:26.714
Do not apologize.

22
00:01:30.568 --> 00:01:32.068
It came from Susan's house.

23
00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.765
- Call 911.
- Josh. no.

24
00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:34.789
Let the cops handle it.

25
00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.159
Just stay here. okay?

26
00:01:46.628 --> 00:01:48.519
Susan?

27
00:01:48.543 --> 00:01:49.761
Susan!

28
00:01:51.894 --> 00:01:53.503
Are you all right?

29
00:02:01.556 --> 00:02:05.429
If there's anybody in
here. cops are on the way!

30
00:02:27.712 --> 00:02:30.517
Susan granwell. dead in the kitchen.

31
00:02:30.541 --> 00:02:32.084
Must have been a pretty
big donor for the mayor

32
00:02:32.108 --> 00:02:33.390
to ask you all to step in.

33
00:02:33.414 --> 00:02:35.522
They were old friends.
What do we know?

34
00:02:35.546 --> 00:02:37.611
Neighbors heard a
commotion around 11:00 P.M.

35
00:02:37.635 --> 00:02:39.613
One of them came to check on Susan.

36
00:02:39.637 --> 00:02:42.399
found her bleeding out on
the ground. already deceased.

37
00:02:42.423 --> 00:02:44.618
Preliminary cause of death is
blunt force trauma to the head.

38
00:02:44.642 --> 00:02:46.968
Looks like she got hit with that cast iron.

39
00:02:46.992 --> 00:02:48.970
Okay. we'll have it sent to
the lab for further processing.

40
00:02:48.994 --> 00:02:49.971
Whose firearm is that?

41
00:02:49.995 --> 00:02:51.930
Registered to the victim.

42
00:02:51.954 --> 00:02:53.912
but csu didn't recover any shell casings.

43
00:02:54.043 --> 00:02:56.543
So she wasn't able to
fire it off before she got hit.

44
00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.197
That skillet's a weapon of opportunity.

45
00:02:58.221 --> 00:02:59.764
so it's not premeditated murder.

46
00:02:59.788 --> 00:03:01.006
What. a robbery gone wrong?

47
00:03:01.137 --> 00:03:02.878
She confronted them with a gun.

48
00:03:03.008 --> 00:03:04.464
they retaliated by grabbing a cast iron?

49
00:03:04.488 --> 00:03:05.707
Maybe.

50
00:03:05.837 --> 00:03:07.641
Nice house. lots of valuables.

51
00:03:07.665 --> 00:03:09.077
Doesn't feel like a break-in.

52
00:03:09.101 --> 00:03:11.297
Only disturbance was in here.

53
00:03:11.321 --> 00:03:13.560
Windows and doors were
intact. Alarm didn't go.

54
00:03:13.584 --> 00:03:15.214
Whoever did this either
had access to the house.

55
00:03:15.238 --> 00:03:17.675
or she let them in.

56
00:03:17.806 --> 00:03:20.088
Looks like a crime of passion.

57
00:03:20.112 --> 00:03:23.527
I have a feeling Susan
granwell knew her killer.

58
00:03:23.551 --> 00:03:25.442
All right. folks. last night. Susan granwell

59
00:03:25.466 --> 00:03:27.748
was attacked and killed in her home.

60
00:03:27.772 --> 00:03:31.535
a $12 million historically
preserved home in fields ton.

61
00:03:31.559 --> 00:03:35.234
Susan was a major donor
and confidant of the mayor.

62
00:03:35.258 --> 00:03:38.174
He would like her killer
brought to justice immediately.

63
00:03:38.305 --> 00:03:39.717
Right. hey. have we
notified the family yet?

64
00:03:39.741 --> 00:03:42.067
No... her son Bobby is in
Tokyo with his grandparents.

65
00:03:42.091 --> 00:03:43.199
and because of the time change.

66
00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.702
we haven't been able to reach them.

67
00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:46.941
But by the time I have to
look this boy in the eyes

68
00:03:46.965 --> 00:03:48.245
and tell him his mother is gone.

69
00:03:48.315 --> 00:03:50.075
I would like to have
some real answers for him.

70
00:03:50.099 --> 00:03:52.188
Our team's initial assessment was that

71
00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:54.321
this looks like a crime of passion.

72
00:03:54.451 --> 00:03:56.386
so let's talk about Susan
granwell and anyone

73
00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.126
in her life who could have
snapped and killed her.

74
00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.389
Right. well. Susan grew up

75
00:03:59.413 --> 00:04:01.434
an Upper East Side socialite. old money.

76
00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:03.784
Now she's a hotelier by way of marriage.

77
00:04:03.808 --> 00:04:06.091
Her late husband. Alex.
founded a chain of boutique hotels

78
00:04:06.115 --> 00:04:07.614
called the granwell hotels.

79
00:04:07.638 --> 00:04:08.659
They have locations across the country.

80
00:04:08.683 --> 00:04:10.182
Yeah. Sam and I
stayed at a granwell once.

81
00:04:10.206 --> 00:04:11.512
They had a pillow menu.

82
00:04:11.642 --> 00:04:13.141
Well. that's not all they got.

83
00:04:13.165 --> 00:04:14.839
Turns out granwell hotels is knee-deep

84
00:04:14.863 --> 00:04:16.362
in a serious labor dispute.

85
00:04:16.386 --> 00:04:17.786
Maintenance and hospitality workers

86
00:04:17.909 --> 00:04:20.932
have been on strike
for the past three months

87
00:04:20.956 --> 00:04:22.586
with no end in sight.

88
00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.327
They claim Susan is
trying to starve them out.

89
00:04:24.351 --> 00:04:25.893
The protests have been peaceful.

90
00:04:25.917 --> 00:04:27.155
but it's getting nasty.

91
00:04:27.179 --> 00:04:29.245
Nasty enough to attack
Susan in her own home?

92
00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.357
She thought so.

93
00:04:30.487 --> 00:04:32.228
Susan filed a police report last week

94
00:04:32.359 --> 00:04:34.337
after a brick was thrown
through her front window.

95
00:04:34.361 --> 00:04:36.188
She blamed her disgruntled employees.

96
00:04:36.319 --> 00:04:38.384
but the cops weren't
able to ID a suspect.

97
00:04:38.408 --> 00:04:40.125
So the brick was to
scare her into returning

98
00:04:40.149 --> 00:04:42.083
to the negotiating table.

99
00:04:42.107 --> 00:04:44.129
When that didn't work. maybe
they amped up the intimidation.

100
00:04:44.153 --> 00:04:45.783
and it got out of hand.

101
00:04:45.807 --> 00:04:47.243
Who's running this union?

102
00:04:47.374 --> 00:04:50.744
That would be Jeremy
Payton. career labor organizer.

103
00:04:50.768 --> 00:04:52.572
known for running
campaigns of intimidation.

104
00:04:52.596 --> 00:04:54.206
He has threatened multiple times

105
00:04:54.337 --> 00:04:55.657
to burn down granwell properties.

106
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.340
Not the type to catch flies with honey?

107
00:04:57.471 --> 00:04:59.362
Definitely not.

108
00:04:59.386 --> 00:05:04.018
Granwell sent their goons to
rough me up. to silence me.

109
00:05:04.042 --> 00:05:06.194
We're not scared of you!

110
00:05:06.218 --> 00:05:07.979
You hear that. Susan?

111
00:05:08.003 --> 00:05:10.111
You should be scared of us!

112
00:05:10.135 --> 00:05:12.244
Well. he might be a charmer.
but if it walks like a motive

113
00:05:12.268 --> 00:05:13.332
and talks like a motive...

114
00:05:13.356 --> 00:05:14.768
well. forensics might back it up.

115
00:05:14.792 --> 00:05:16.204
Yeah?

116
00:05:16.228 --> 00:05:17.771
Report from the crime scene just landed.

117
00:05:17.795 --> 00:05:19.556
and Jeremy's fingerprints
were found all over it.

118
00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.016
Low lipid oxidation

119
00:05:21.146 --> 00:05:23.429
in the residue suggests
his prints were recent.

120
00:05:23.453 --> 00:05:24.996
- What about the murder weapon?
- Wiped clean.

121
00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.084
No fingerprints there.

122
00:05:26.108 --> 00:05:27.520
Well. nice try. Jeremy.

123
00:05:27.544 --> 00:05:28.913
The man was there.

124
00:05:28.937 --> 00:05:32.375
Let's bring him in.

125
00:05:32.506 --> 00:05:35.702
Granwell. granwell. you can't hide!

126
00:05:35.726 --> 00:05:38.357
We can see your greedy side!

127
00:05:38.381 --> 00:05:41.360
Granwell. granwell. you can't hide!

128
00:05:41.384 --> 00:05:43.057
- We can see your greedy side!
- Back up. scabs!

129
00:05:43.081 --> 00:05:45.606
Nobody's getting through this picket line!

130
00:05:45.736 --> 00:05:47.540
Get out of here! Boo!

131
00:05:47.564 --> 00:05:51.022
Scab!

132
00:05:51.046 --> 00:05:52.197
Excuse me. FBI. Excuse us.

133
00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.463
Jeremy Payton. how you doing?

134
00:05:57.487 --> 00:05:58.986
Why don't we take the
temperature down a little bit?

135
00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.840
Law enforcement protecting
the corporate fat cats again!

136
00:06:02.971 --> 00:06:05.166
Why am I not surprised?

137
00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.429
No. No. wait.

138
00:06:06.453 --> 00:06:08.474
That's not what's happening here. okay?

139
00:06:08.498 --> 00:06:10.258
Look. Mr. Payton. we have
a few questions for you.

140
00:06:10.282 --> 00:06:13.764
so why don't you come with us?

141
00:06:13.895 --> 00:06:15.984
Obstructing a federal
agent is a crime. fellas.

142
00:06:16.114 --> 00:06:18.484
So move. Now.

143
00:06:18.508 --> 00:06:20.641
You don't tell them
what to do. sweetheart.

144
00:06:20.771 --> 00:06:21.859
Sweetheart?

145
00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:22.923
Okay. yeah. no. that's not gonna work.

146
00:06:22.947 --> 00:06:24.403
Let's go.

147
00:06:24.427 --> 00:06:25.839
You two. step aside. or you're coming.

148
00:06:25.863 --> 00:06:27.058
Let's go. Hands behind your back.

149
00:06:27.082 --> 00:06:29.626
See? You see what they're doing to us?

150
00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:32.653
Don't let these jackboots
take away your voices!

151
00:06:32.783 --> 00:06:39.113
Union strong!

152
00:06:39.137 --> 00:06:40.593
You hear that. Susan?

153
00:06:40.617 --> 00:06:42.053
You should be scared...

154
00:06:44.969 --> 00:06:46.860
from the moment I saw you guys.

155
00:06:46.884 --> 00:06:48.384
I knew that this was what it was about.

156
00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:49.994
That's not what you were screaming

157
00:06:50.018 --> 00:06:51.474
at your union brethren about.

158
00:06:51.498 --> 00:06:53.171
You wanted them to
believe that we were there

159
00:06:53.195 --> 00:06:54.651
to shut down your picket.

160
00:06:54.675 --> 00:06:57.480
I saw an opportunity to
keep my people angry.

161
00:06:57.504 --> 00:06:59.525
energized. and I took it.

162
00:06:59.549 --> 00:07:03.573
Sure. it was theater. but so was this.

163
00:07:03.597 --> 00:07:05.662
Nothing I said on that video was real.

164
00:07:05.686 --> 00:07:07.098
So granwell hotels never sent you

165
00:07:07.122 --> 00:07:08.491
their people to beat you up?

166
00:07:08.515 --> 00:07:10.754
Not physically. but you know.

167
00:07:10.778 --> 00:07:12.364
they've been beating
us down for long enough.

168
00:07:12.388 --> 00:07:14.129
Jeremy. please. stop.

169
00:07:14.259 --> 00:07:16.673
All right? That's enough.

170
00:07:16.697 --> 00:07:20.372
Did you fake these injuries.
file a false police report

171
00:07:20.396 --> 00:07:22.330
blaming Susan
granwell's private security?

172
00:07:22.354 --> 00:07:24.898
You gotta give them an
enemy to keep them motivated.

173
00:07:24.922 --> 00:07:27.901
So yeah. I had a couple
of my boys rough me up.

174
00:07:27.925 --> 00:07:29.381
Blamed it all on management.

175
00:07:29.405 --> 00:07:31.078
Sounds like a felony.

176
00:07:31.102 --> 00:07:33.254
Well. it worked.

177
00:07:33.278 --> 00:07:34.604
Momentum's on our side now.

178
00:07:34.628 --> 00:07:37.128
So if Susan granwell is losing.

179
00:07:37.152 --> 00:07:38.608
why'd you pay her a visit?

180
00:07:38.632 --> 00:07:41.045
Your fingerprints. they're
all over Susan's home.

181
00:07:42.374 --> 00:07:44.962
Doorknobs. kitchen counters.

182
00:07:44.986 --> 00:07:48.400
Question is. are we gonna
find them on Susan's body?

183
00:07:48.424 --> 00:07:49.730
Hold up. her body?

184
00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.577
- You killed her.
- Wait. I...

185
00:07:51.601 --> 00:07:53.492
beat her to death and
then fled. did you not?

186
00:07:53.516 --> 00:07:55.058
Whoa... what are you talking about?

187
00:07:55.082 --> 00:07:56.452
No. no. no. no. no. I didn't...

188
00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:59.237
what? No.

189
00:07:59.261 --> 00:08:00.978
No. no. susie.

190
00:08:01.002 --> 00:08:02.002
That's my susie.

191
00:08:03.352 --> 00:08:04.353
Your susie?

192
00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:06.592
I didn't do this. I would never.

193
00:08:06.616 --> 00:08:08.246
I mean. we... we
couldn't come out publicly.

194
00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:09.401
but we were in love.

195
00:08:09.532 --> 00:08:11.641
This woman was your sworn enemy.

196
00:08:11.665 --> 00:08:13.077
You trash talked her daily.

197
00:08:13.101 --> 00:08:14.905
For show.

198
00:08:14.929 --> 00:08:18.343
From the second we met
at negotiations. I felt a spark.

199
00:08:18.367 --> 00:08:21.433
We... we were the same. stubborn.

200
00:08:21.457 --> 00:08:23.372
We wanted big things. you know?

201
00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:25.176
We just chose different paths.

202
00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.744
But that didn't stop the fates
from bringing us together.

203
00:08:27.768 --> 00:08:30.398
It's a good story. but you know.

204
00:08:30.422 --> 00:08:32.183
you've also proven
that you're a good actor.

205
00:08:32.207 --> 00:08:33.207
It's not acting.

206
00:08:33.294 --> 00:08:34.707
Prove it.

207
00:08:37.342 --> 00:08:39.388
I proposed. How about that?

208
00:08:40.998 --> 00:08:44.195
With my nan's heirloom ring.

209
00:08:44.219 --> 00:08:46.110
You can check the
pics on my cell phone.

210
00:08:46.134 --> 00:08:47.546
There's proof there.

211
00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.790
I didn't do this!

212
00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.550
I...

213
00:08:56.448 --> 00:08:57.528
hey. Take a look at that.

214
00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:00.690
Happy family.

215
00:09:00.714 --> 00:09:01.691
Doesn't mean he's innocent. though.

216
00:09:01.715 --> 00:09:03.238
No. but his alibi does.

217
00:09:03.368 --> 00:09:04.998
The joc confirmed via security cams

218
00:09:05.022 --> 00:09:06.391
that Jeremy was at the union office

219
00:09:06.415 --> 00:09:07.455
at the time of the murder.

220
00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:08.785
Well. he's also claiming that

221
00:09:08.809 --> 00:09:10.003
the two of them were engaged.

222
00:09:10.027 --> 00:09:11.594
so that would explain his fingerprints

223
00:09:11.725 --> 00:09:13.224
all over Susan's house.

224
00:09:13.248 --> 00:09:15.313
Yeah. yeah. yeah. but
that engagement ring.

225
00:09:15.337 --> 00:09:16.337
that seems to be missing.

226
00:09:17.731 --> 00:09:19.230
So what. you're saying that this

227
00:09:19.254 --> 00:09:20.666
could be a robbery after all.

228
00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:21.537
and Susan was killed over a ring?

229
00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:22.668
It's possible. right?

230
00:09:22.692 --> 00:09:24.235
Yeah.

231
00:09:24.259 --> 00:09:26.498
I looked into vintage
rings like this for Nina.

232
00:09:26.522 --> 00:09:30.023
and a rock like that from
the '20s. good clarity.

233
00:09:30.047 --> 00:09:32.635
thing would go for 750k easy.

234
00:09:32.659 --> 00:09:34.680
Thanks. Elise. Well. you win.

235
00:09:34.704 --> 00:09:36.532
but by "price is right" rules.

236
00:09:36.663 --> 00:09:39.859
Jeremy's insurance policy
puts the ring's value at 800k.

237
00:09:39.883 --> 00:09:41.842
Okay. yeah. someone might kill over that.

238
00:09:41.972 --> 00:09:43.602
- Yeah. for sure.
- Okay. but Jeremy said

239
00:09:43.626 --> 00:09:45.778
that only the people in this photo

240
00:09:45.802 --> 00:09:47.848
knew about the engagement.

241
00:09:47.978 --> 00:09:49.347
Well. that's not entirely true.

242
00:09:49.371 --> 00:09:51.373
Someone took this picture.

243
00:09:53.854 --> 00:09:55.483
All right. so according to Jeremy Payton.

244
00:09:55.507 --> 00:09:58.530
Bobby's private math tutor
took this photo. which means.

245
00:09:58.554 --> 00:10:00.837
if true. this tutor is the
only other person we know

246
00:10:00.861 --> 00:10:03.579
knew our victim had an $800.000 ring.

247
00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:05.058
- Which is now missing.
- Right.

248
00:10:05.082 --> 00:10:07.084
And Jeremy also said the tutor

249
00:10:07.215 --> 00:10:08.366
had a key to Susan's home.

250
00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:10.673
So that is means. that is opportunity.

251
00:10:10.697 --> 00:10:12.892
and that's me hoping you
figure out who this tutor is.

252
00:10:12.916 --> 00:10:14.851
Lucas Williams. 18.

253
00:10:14.875 --> 00:10:16.659
lives in corona with his dad. frank.

254
00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.071
and younger sister. faith.

255
00:10:18.095 --> 00:10:20.247
Okay. Ian. you wanna
get up on his phone?

256
00:10:20.271 --> 00:10:21.969
- On it.
- Any criminal history?

257
00:10:22.099 --> 00:10:24.208
- Not even a parking ticket.
- He's an impressive kid.

258
00:10:24.232 --> 00:10:25.775
Was up for the Miller-dier prize

259
00:10:25.799 --> 00:10:27.733
in high school computing last year.

260
00:10:27.757 --> 00:10:29.735
He's an honor student at the
Augustus school in Manhattan.

